  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "What is the constant term in the expression $\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{4}{9}-w+\\frac{1}{5}x?$",
  "worked_solution": "The expression has four terms: $\\frac{1}{6}y$, $-\\frac{4}{9}$, $-w$ and $\\frac{1}{5}x.$ The only term that does not contain any variables is $-\\frac{4}{9}$, so $-\\frac{4}{9}$ is the constant term.",
